   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It has not been a problem in the cases I&#39;ve examined: proceed with caution. If some variances are missing a model can be re-fitted with model = &#39;none&#39; and start=previousmodelfit. <br></div><div><br></div><div>You seem to be trying to fit an exhaustive list of detection models. What about all the combinations involving variation in sigma? Basically, I think this is not good practice.<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Fri, Nov 16, 2018 at 4:41 AM Amael Hinojo Antille &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">amael...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
